course: dictionary
lesson: 2012
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. «She rubbed conditioner through her hair after shampoo.» The clues are hair and shampoo, so conditioner here is a creamy liquid that makes hair soft.
explain: «The air conditioner kept the classroom cool all afternoon.» Air and cool are the clues, so this conditioner is a machine. Ask yourself: what meaning fits here? Then put that meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Mum added fabric conditioner to the washing machine.» Washing and machine are the clues, so fabric conditioner must be a liquid that makes clothes soft. Gardeners use soil conditioner in the same way, to improve the ground.
fact: Conditioner is a noun, and its plural is conditioners.
fact: «Conditioner» can mean any substance that improves something, such as soil conditioner or leather conditioner.
fact: «Air conditioner» is short for a machine that cools the air in a room.
fact: In the US, fabric conditioner is called fabric softener.
fact: An air conditioner works like a fridge for a room: it takes heat from inside and pushes it out through a box outside.
exercise: «Tomas rubbed conditioner through his wet hair so it would comb easily.» What is conditioner here? | *A creamy liquid that makes hair soft and smooth | A machine that cools a room | A tool for brushing teeth | A cloth for drying dishes
exercise: «The air conditioner in the shop kept everyone cool all afternoon.» What does air conditioner mean? | *A machine that cools the air in a room | A liquid for soft clothes | A cloth for drying dishes | A special soap for hands
exercise: «Dad dug soil conditioner into the vegetable bed.» What does soil conditioner do? | *It improves the soil so plants grow better | It cools the soil in summer | It turns soil into bricks | It turns soil into water
test: «Mum put fabric conditioner in the washing machine so the towels would smell nice.» What is fabric conditioner? | A powder for killing weeds | A paint for walls | *A liquid that makes clothes soft and fresh-smelling | A soap for cleaning shoes
test: «Air conditioners drip water outside because cooling the air turns some of its water vapour into droplets.» Why do air conditioners drip? | They are filled with water to cool down | Rain keeps falling on them | *Cooling the air turns some water vapour into droplets | They leak from broken pipes on purpose
exam: «Fridges and air conditioners use special gases that soak up heat when they evaporate.» What do these special gases do? | *They soak up heat when they evaporate | They make the room warm | They turn into paper when they are cold | They make the air sticky and wet
